// Rule: [T1059.003][T1105] Bluemoon - Browser CMD Curl Chain
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.003, T1105
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Detects curl.exe writing beneath T emp when launched by cmd.exe whose parent is a Chromium-family browser-the distinctive process tree reported for default BlueMoon exploitation.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for browser cmd curl chain using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: Boundary: A match does not prove browser exploitation, payload execution, actor attribution, or compromise.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// BlueMoon browser -> cmd.exe -> curl.exe process chain
// Status: Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint / DeviceProcessEvents
// Evidence: Proofpoint directly reported chrome.exe -> cmd.exe -> curl.exe and
// the default curl download to %TEMP% followed by execution.
// Boundary: A match does not prove browser exploitation, payload execution,
// actor attribution, or compromise. Validate browser provenance and destination.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "curl.exe"
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "cmd.exe"
| where InitiatingProcessParentFileName in~ ("chrome.exe", "msedge.exe", "brave.exe", "vivaldi.exe")
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "-o"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains @"\Temp\"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountDomain, AccountName,
    FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine, ProcessId, ProcessUniqueId,
    InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessParentFileName, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
